@startuml edicao-imagem-sequence

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 150
skinparam participantPadding 10
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  BorderColor #FBC02D
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #455A64
  LifeLineBorderColor #607D8B
  ParticipantBorderColor #37474F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #CFD8DC
}

title Fluxo de edição de imagem — caminho feliz (200 PNG)

participant "Cliente HTTP" as Cliente

box "Camada Web" #EEEEEE
  participant "ImageEditController\n(web)" as Controller
end box

box "Camada de Serviço" #E8F5E9
  participant "ImageEditService\n(service)" as Service
  participant "ImageResizer\n(service)" as Resizer
end box

box "Camada de IA (gateway)" #E3F2FD
  participant "OpenAiRestClientImageEditModel\n(ai)" as Gateway
end box

participant "OpenAI API\n/v1/images/edits" as OpenAI

Cliente -> Controller : 1. POST /images/edit\n(multipart/form-data, campo "image" = foto do ambiente)
Controller -> Controller : 2. image.getBytes()\n(extrai bytes do MultipartFile)
Controller -> Service : 3. generate(byte[] ambiente)
Service -> Service : 4. carrega pedra do disco\n(FileSystemResource(props.getStonePath()).getContentAsByteArray())
note over Service
  A imagem da pedra (granito) vem de
  props.getStonePath(), configuravel em
  application.yaml. Nao e enviada pelo cliente.
end note
Service -> Resizer : 5. resize(ambiente)
Resizer --> Service : ambiente redimensionado (JPEG <= 1536px)
Service -> Service : 6. monta ImageEditPrompt\n(EditPrompts.COUNTERTOP + AiImageOptions.defaults()\n+ InputImage[ambiente, pedra])
Service -> Gateway : 7. model.call(prompt)
Gateway -> Gateway : 8. monta multipart\n(image[0] = ambiente, image[1] = pedra)
note over Gateway
  A ordem das duas partes image[] e semantica:
  image[0] = ambiente (IMAGE 1),
  image[1] = pedra/granito (IMAGE 2).
  O prompt fixo EditPrompts.COUNTERTOP referencia
  essa ordem.
end note
Gateway -> OpenAI : 9. POST /v1/images/edits\n(multipart, Authorization Bearer)
OpenAI --> Gateway : 10. 200 OK\nJSON com data[0].b64_json (+ usage)
Gateway -> Gateway : 11. traduz JSON em ImageResponse\n(results, metadata, raw)
Gateway --> Service : 12. retorna ImageResponse
Service -> Service : 13. traduz em\nGenerateResult.Ok(b64, raw, usage, latencyMs)
note over Service
  O service traduz o contrato do gateway
  (que lanca AiImageException em falha) em
  GenerateResult.Ok/Err (sealed). O controller
  nunca recebe excecao do service.
end note
Service --> Controller : 14. retorna GenerateResult.Ok
Controller -> Controller : 15. Base64.getDecoder().decode(ok.b64())\n(base64 -> bytes PNG)
Controller --> Cliente : 16. 200 OK\n(Content-Type: image/png, body PNG)

@enduml
